There is a lot of different type of refinements in the end. 
Using the template.item hook and passing a function that returns a template is totally possible, but because of the multiple filter type `disjunctive`, `numerical` there is a lot of use case to manage, and it doesn't feel as the most efficient way to do it, just in order to display the `attributeName` in addition to the refined value.

```js
search.addWidget(
    instantsearch.widgets.currentRefinedValues({
      container: '#active-filters',
      clearAll: 'after',
      transformData: function(data) {
        console.log(data);
        return data;
      },
      templates: {
        item: function(item) {
          var html = '';
          if (item.type === 'disjunctive' && item.name === 'false') {
            html = '';
          }
          else {
            html = `<span class="ais-current-refined-values--attribute-name">${item.attributeName}</span>: <span class="ais-current-refined-values--name">${item.name}</span> <span class="ais-current-refined-values--count">(${item.count})</span>`;
          }

          return html;
        }
      }
    })
  );
```

